Z||000000||firstfiero||03-21-2001||10:26 AM||||    Just wanted to know if it was worth the 30 bucks or not. How long does it last?  ||||reg||5
Z||000001||RDosdorian||03-21-2001||11:01 AM||||If this is the video I purchased from them about two years ago, my opinion is it's NOT worth the $30.  Maybe $10 would be more like it.  All the video is, is a copy of the episode of "Motor Week" that included the Fiero in 1988.  Don't waste your money.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.goldengatefieros.org/RDosdorian_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||ChadMan||03-21-2001||11:20 AM||||Whether it's worth the $30 depends on whether you're interested in Fieros more as a collector or a tuner/racer.  Admittedly, the price is steep for a 45-minute Motorweek video and there's nothing in there about racing Fieros, aftermarket improvements to Fieros, or engine swaps.<P>That said, I think it's worth the money because it's a great historical document of stock Fiero evolution.  The video includes the following:<P>* 1983 preview piece on the '84 Fiero<BR>* Road test of a beautiful red '84 SE<BR>* Track test of a red 85 GT automatic at Pocono Raceway<BR>* Road test of a black 86 GT 4-sp<BR>* Track test of red 88 GT and yellow Formula at Mid-Ohio Sports Car Course.  Includes footage of 88 power steering system being demonstrated.<BR>* Comparison test of a white Formula 5-sp vs. a red supercharged MR2.  The Fiero is slightly slower but the Motorweek editors preferred it to the MR2 overall.<BR>* Announcement of Fiero being discontinued<p>[This message has been edited by ChadMan (edited 03-21-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000003||Bob Englert||03-21-2001||12:46 PM||||One thing I found interesting about the video is the change in attitude about the Fiero.  They raved about the handling in 83-84, later they complained about it.  <P>The opinion shift was quite interesting IMO.<P><BR>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl<p>[This message has been edited by Bob Englert (edited 03-21-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||firstfiero||03-21-2001||12:58 PM||||   I'm more interested in the historical aspect so it sounds good to me!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
